{"id": "tea:naiskarmyasiddhi:1", "source": "src:naiskarmyasiddhi", "location": {"ref": "1"}, "paraphrase": "Works, whether alone or combined with knowledge, cannot bring liberation, which is the self's eternal nature; works purify the mind and turn it inward, and are then left behind — they are not co-causes with knowledge.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "action"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "dispute"], "concepts": ["cpt:karma-in-advaita"], "disputes": ["dsp:jnana-karma-samuccaya", "dsp:works-knowledge-grace"], "notes": "Chapter-level.", "teachers": ["tch:suresvara"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:naiskarmyasiddhi:2", "source": "src:naiskarmyasiddhi", "location": {"ref": "2"}, "paraphrase": "By the method of agreement and difference (anvaya-vyatireka) — the self persists through waking, dream and sleep while the body, senses and mind come and go — the self is separated from the not-self.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice", "consciousness-mind"], "practices": ["prc:anvaya-vyatireka", "prc:avastha-traya-viveka"], "notes": "Chapter-level.", "teachers": ["tch:suresvara"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:naiskarmyasiddhi:3", "source": "src:naiskarmyasiddhi", "location": {"ref": "3"}, "paraphrase": "The sentence 'tat tvam asi', its word-meanings purified by exclusion of contradictory elements, gives immediate knowledge of the inner self as Brahman; no further act (meditation) is needed to make it effective.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["sound-language", "karma-liberation"], "terms": ["trm:tat-tvam-asi", "trm:laksana"], "concepts": ["cpt:mahavakya"], "disputes": ["dsp:sravana-alone-liberates", "dsp:prasankhyana"], "notes": "Chapter-level.", "teachers": ["tch:suresvara"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:naiskarmyasiddhi:4.62", "source": "src:naiskarmyasiddhi", "location": {"ref": "4.62"}, "original": {"text": "buddhādvaitasatattvasya yatheṣṭācaraṇaṃ yadi / śunāṃ tattvadṛśāṃ caiva ko bhedo 'śucibhakṣaṇe", "script": "IAST", "edition": "vulgate wording recalled from memory (verify against an edition)", "licence": "public domain (pre-modern text)"}, "paraphrase": "If one who has understood the truth of non-duality could behave as he pleases, what difference would there be between the knowers of truth and dogs in eating impure things?", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["ethics"], "concepts": ["cpt:jivanmukta-marks"], "teachers": ["tch:suresvara"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:naiskarmyasiddhi:4.69", "source": "src:naiskarmyasiddhi", "location": {"ref": "4.69"}, "original": {"text": "utpannātmaprabodhasya tv adveṣṭṛtvādayo guṇāḥ / ayatnato bhavanty asya na tu sādhanarūpiṇaḥ", "script": "IAST", "edition": "vulgate wording recalled from memory (verify against an edition)", "licence": "public domain (pre-modern text)"}, "paraphrase": "In one in whom knowledge of the self has arisen, non-hatred and the other virtues occur without effort; they are no longer means (to be practised).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["ethics", "powers-experiences"], "concepts": ["cpt:jivanmukta-marks"], "teachers": ["tch:suresvara"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
